From aef9be9710b3a6d13b7761161fad80c7e7cfa3b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:02:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make the shipped agent docs and the lefthook gate
 actually work
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- lefthook.yml was inert: lefthook was not a dependency and nothing ran
  `lefthook install`, so a fresh clone bypassed every gate this PR adds.
  Added the devDependency and a `prepare` script.
- docs/agents/forge-workflow.md (and the five harness files generated from
  it) told agents to run `scripts/beads-context.sh`, which does not exist in
  this repo. Replaced with the `bd` commands that do.
- .claude/commands/validate.md pointed at `bun run check`, `scripts/validate.sh`
  and `bun run typecheck` — none of which exist. Pointed at lefthook and
  `bun run type-check`.
- .claude/commands/verify.md force-removed a worktree in a step that describes
  itself as read-only; dropped `--force` so uncommitted work is never discarded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
